  "summary": "Business Intelligence= love[1]; app-analysis&tuning= love[2]; guitar, lapidary, farming= love[3].  Family and grandkids= love[0].   Greatful participant in many apps he has designed/coded/maintained for early micro prototypes in 6502 asm with multi-key ISAM local storage in 1982, software for the LISA, the first Macintosh, the first Internet apps, to the first Business Intelligence tools; the JS revolution... all the way thru the cool SPA JS and C#/rails/node/mongo/angular/react/SQL/noSQL/FHIR solutions of today.   \n\nProjects in Cupertino with Apple and Corvus, Random House, Terrapin Logo, LifeTouch, SCVIR, Brown University, StayWell; they've all allowed me to learn what should be able to be done by when, for how much.  But even more, they've showed me 'why', and 'so what', what's likely to work, what's likely to not work, and what truly matters.\n\nOver the years, the skill that has seemed to be the most compelling acquisition is learning how to inspire a similar passion in others. \n\nImproving communication efficiency, seeding a thirst for creating.  Not just the New. The truly better, the truly improved; the truly fun attitude that encourages mutual confidence, respect, and growth by teaching others to better our lives with technology.  This drives me.",
